From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:28:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: Translate ResourceDescriptorHeap and
 SamplerDescriptorHeap.

Shader Model 6.6 dynamic resources (createHandleFromHeap, op 218) were
refused. Each distinct ResourceProperties that annotateHandle gives a
createHandleFromHeap handle now becomes a resource range of its own: register
space ~0u, lower bound 0, unbounded, range IDs from 1 << 24, class, kind,
element type, stride and flags decoded from the properties. The heap index is
its register, so a heap load is the table load at the heap's descriptor
index.

The root arguments carry the heaps. When a root signature has
CBV_SRV_UAV_HEAP_DIRECTLY_INDEXED (0x400) or SAMPLER_HEAP_DIRECTLY_INDEXED
(0x800), two qwords follow the last parameter's: the CBV/SRV/UAV heap's GPU
descriptor base, then the sampler heap's. setup_binding_rootsig declares them
(fields heap and sampler_heap) only in a shader with heap ranges, and maps the
view heap's ranges to the first and the sampler heap's to the second, at
descriptor offset 0. A heap-indexing shader with no root signature, or whose
root signature lacks the flag its heap needs, is refused naming the flag.
RootSignatureFlags reads a root signature blob's flags.

A 64-bit groupshared atomic (an atomicrmw or cmpxchg of i64 on addrspace(3),
which no dx.op carries) is refused when the shader is initialized, naming the
instruction: Metal has no threadgroup ulong atomics, and its compiler service
crashes on them, slowly and without naming them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
